/target
# The directory's *contents*, not the directory: excluding a directory
# outright is the one exclusion git will not let a nested file re-include, and
# `.codeatlas/.gitignore` (ADR-0007) has to be able to publish the annotation
# store. Everything in here stays ignored by default either way. The `**/`
# keeps the old pattern's reach — a scan run from a subdirectory leaves a
# `.codeatlas/` there too.
**/.codeatlas/*
node_modules/
dashboard/dist/
dashboard/dist-egress/
